CLI Utility (curl + jq)

This document describes a command-line utility that allows support engineers to execute Black Duck SCA API calls defined in the official Postman Collection using only curl, jq, and the Postman Collection JSON.

The goal is to:
	•	Avoid Postman entirely
	•	Be transparent and debuggable
	•	Be easy to extend by support engineers
	•	Match how the Black Duck APIs are actually called

⸻

1. What This Utility Is (and Is Not)

This is:
	•	A shell-based utility (bash/zsh compatible)
	•	A thin execution layer over the Postman Collection JSON
	•	A support-focused testing tool, not a full SDK

This is not:
	•	A language SDK
	•	A full API abstraction layer
	•	A replacement for official documentation

Think of this as a Postman runner for the CLI.

